Ah! I see - `apply_data_column_sidecar` is called ONLY for accepted sidecars (after all validation passes). The inner HashMap DOES store `block_root -> commitments`, which means it distinguishes between different block roots.

Let me re-examine the dedup check at line 2096-2102:

```rust
if self.accepted_data_column_sidecars.contains_key(&(
    block_header.slot,
    block_header.proposer_index,
    data_column_sidecar.index,
)) && !block_seen
{
    return Ok(DataColumnSidecarAction::Ignore(true));
}
```

This only checks if the OUTER key exists, not if the specific `(block_root, commitments)` pair exists. So if ANY sidecar for `(slot, proposer, index)` has been accepted, this will trigger for ALL subsequent sidecars with the same tuple, regardless of their block_root or commitments.

But wait - there's a condition `&& !block_seen`. What does `block_seen` mean? Let me check:

